  "description": "Indiana's 2nd Congressional District general election pits Republican incumbent Rudy Yakym against Democratic nominee Jamee Decio. The district covers northern Indiana, including Elkhart, South Bend, and parts of 11 counties. Yakym, first elected in a 2022 special election following the death of Rep. Jackie Walorski, is seeking a second full term on a platform of conservative fiscal policies and federal bureaucracy reduction. Decio, an attorney and former screenwriter, is campaigning on affordability, healthcare access, and opposition to current immigration enforcement policies. The race offers voters a clear contrast on federal spending, immigration, and the role of government.",
